#### Scenario 2: Dark Launch for Load Testing

**Situation:** New claims validation service needs performance validation with production load before cutover from legacy service. Team wants to run both services in parallel, measuring performance without impacting production claims processing.

**Flag Implementation:**
```yaml
flag_key: claims-validation-service-v2
name: Claims Validation Service V2
description: |
  Dark launch of new validation service.
  Runs in parallel with legacy service but results not used.

variations:

  - dark_launch: Run new service, use legacy results
  - full_cutover: Use new service results

targeting:
  production:
    # Dark launch mode - run new service but don't use results
    default_variation: dark_launch
```

**Code Implementation:**
```csharp
public async Task<ValidationResult> ValidateClaim(Claim claim)
{
    var flagValue = _flagClient.StringVariation(
        "claims-validation-service-v2",
        CreateUserContext(claim),
        "legacy_only"
    );

    // Always call legacy service (current production system)
    var legacyResult = await _legacyValidationService.Validate(claim);

    if (flagValue == "dark_launch")
    {
        // Call new service in parallel but don't wait or use results
        _ = Task.Run(async () =>
        {
            try
            {
                var newResult = await _newValidationService.Validate(claim);

                // Log for comparison analysis
                _metrics.LogDarkLaunch(
                    claimId: claim.Id,
                    legacyResult: legacyResult,
                    newResult: newResult,
                    matchesLegacy: legacyResult.IsValid == newResult.IsValid
                );
            }
            catch (Exception ex)
            {
                _logger.LogWarning(ex, "Dark launch validation failed");
            }
        });
    }
    else if (flagValue == "full_cutover")
    {
        // Use new service results
        return await _newValidationService.Validate(claim);
    }

    // Return legacy results (dark launch mode)
    return legacyResult;
}
```

**Benefits:**
- ✅ Validate performance with real production load
- ✅ Compare results between old and new service
- ✅ Zero impact on production claims processing
- ✅ Build confidence before cutover
